WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.789
Fine-tuning datasets that pass the first time: JSONL, formats and token

2
00:00:05.789 --> 00:00:06.340
budgets.

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.051
The shapes of a fine-tuning file, the mistakes that fail a training job,

4
00:00:12.051 --> 00:00:16.672
how to convert between formats and count the cost, all checked in your browser.

5
00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:23.177
What a fine-tuning file is. Almost every trainer reads JSONL: plain text

6
00:00:23.177 --> 00:00:25.304
with one JSON object per line.

7
00:00:26.604 --> 00:00:30.487
The mistakes that fail a job. Most failures come from a short list.

8
00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:34.232
Making many examples from one template.

9
00:00:34.232 --> 00:00:39.373
A lot of good training data starts as a template and a table: the same instruction

10
00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:43.072
with a different product, customer or question on each row.

11
00:00:44.372 --> 00:00:48.449
Split, then check again. Keep part of the data back to see whether the model

12
00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:49.791
really learned something.

13
00:00:51.091 --> 00:00:54.760
To try it, open Fine-tune Dataset Checker in OpenFile.

14
00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.633
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:02.099
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:04.191 --> 00:01:07.881
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
